WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.019 --> 00:00:03.538
I'm listening to your beautiful accent.

00:00:03.538 --> 00:00:08.158
But, is it true that the
late Great John Singleton,

00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:13.158
that he had you come out here
to do something with the role?

00:00:14.308 --> 00:00:15.808
- [Damson] That's true.

00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:17.908
By audition number eight,

00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:20.398
Singleton took me to South-Central,

00:00:20.398 --> 00:00:23.158
opened the car door and
said, if you survive,

00:00:23.158 --> 00:00:24.396
you've got the role.

00:00:24.396 --> 00:00:26.668
(audience laughs)
(Damson laughs)

00:00:26.668 --> 00:00:28.288
And it really was an experience.

00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.668
You know, I was walking
around South Central.

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:31.438
I had to stay in character,

00:00:31.438 --> 00:00:33.088
so I wasn't allowed to be British.

00:00:33.088 --> 00:00:35.315
And I said to his mother,

00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:37.018
"Oh, how lovely your hair looks today.

00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:39.058
I'm just gonna go and, you know, put some,

00:00:39.058 --> 00:00:40.138
put this in a bin."

00:00:40.138 --> 00:00:43.048
And she goes, "John! He
ain't from here, huh?"

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:44.998
- [Drew] Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:44.998 --> 00:00:45.988
- Nearly lost the part.

00:00:45.988 --> 00:00:47.188
But hey, six seasons later.

00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:48.492
Here we are.

00:00:48.492 --> 00:00:49.788
(audience applause)
- Six seasons later.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.146
And this is the final season, right?

00:00:54.146 --> 00:00:55.118
- Yeah.

00:00:55.118 --> 00:00:57.118
- And I didn't know this.

00:00:57.118 --> 00:00:57.958
Is this true?

00:00:57.958 --> 00:01:00.575
That you are friends
with Jay-Z and Beyonce?

00:01:00.575 --> 00:01:02.760
(Damson laughs)

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.049
(audience applause)

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:05.375
- Yeah, I...

00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:06.745
I've been 'round them many times. Yes.

00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:07.578
- [Drew] Oh, my God.

00:01:07.578 --> 00:01:08.788
What are they like?

00:01:08.788 --> 00:01:11.828
Because like, they're very
embracing of you, right?

00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:12.661
- [Damson] Yeah.

00:01:12.661 --> 00:01:16.088
- Like, he's like paternal,
basically, with you a bit.

00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:18.568
- Yeah, I- I'll be in Miami,

00:01:18.568 --> 00:01:20.855
it's late, and I'll call
them up and I'll be like,

00:01:20.855 --> 00:01:24.329
"Hey, I can't get a
reservation at Carbone.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:26.758
(laughter)

00:01:26.758 --> 00:01:27.928
And then he went, "Damn, see.

00:01:27.928 --> 00:01:29.908
You gotta win a couple more Emmys

00:01:29.908 --> 00:01:31.895
before you can call me at 11:30."

00:01:31.895 --> 00:01:35.098
(laughter)
(audience applause)

00:01:35.098 --> 00:01:36.348
But they're the sweetest.

00:01:37.435 --> 00:01:39.028
We connected in many ways.

00:01:39.028 --> 00:01:41.578
But the Super Bowl was
really great because,

00:01:41.578 --> 00:01:44.008
it was like the first time
I kind of connected with,

00:01:44.008 --> 00:01:47.128
with B, and you know, I
had just walked for Prada,

00:01:47.128 --> 00:01:49.228
which was huge. Such a huge moment for me.

00:01:49.228 --> 00:01:50.896
- [Drew] And aren't you wearing Prada now?

00:01:50.896 --> 00:01:51.866
- [Damson] I am.

00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:54.211
(audience whoops)
(audience applause)

00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:55.348
- And it's looking real good.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.308
- I need a new campaign.

00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:57.504
Thank you for that plug.

00:01:57.504 --> 00:01:59.848
(laughter)

00:01:59.848 --> 00:02:02.548
- And I know that you
have a close connection

00:02:02.548 --> 00:02:04.704
with your sister, is it? I believe?

00:02:04.704 --> 00:02:05.878
- (laughs) Yes.

00:02:05.878 --> 00:02:08.938
- [Drew] And you have a special
connection with tuxedos?

00:02:08.938 --> 00:02:09.771
- Yes.

00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:13.798
- And, is it true that your sister

00:02:13.798 --> 00:02:15.976
did something with you in a tuxedo?

00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:17.278
(Damson laughs)

00:02:17.278 --> 00:02:18.628
- So, when I was a kid, right?

00:02:18.628 --> 00:02:20.668
Like 4, 5, 6 years old,

00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:22.948
my mother would always
dress me in these tuxedos

00:02:22.948 --> 00:02:23.984
for my birthday.

00:02:23.984 --> 00:02:24.817
- The cutest.

00:02:24.817 --> 00:02:26.245
- The cutest, yes,

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:29.548
but what was borderline
insane, was my sister,

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:32.581
she would make me marry her doll, Wendy.

00:02:33.598 --> 00:02:34.431
Yes.
(audience laughs)

00:02:34.431 --> 00:02:35.458
- [Drew] Well, in...
- I got married many times.

00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:37.138
- In honor of your sister,

00:02:37.138 --> 00:02:40.498
would you ever consider marrying a doll

00:02:40.498 --> 00:02:42.745
in a tuxedo, right now?

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:46.387
(Drew chuckles)
(audience whoops)

00:02:46.387 --> 00:02:48.536
(Damson chuckles nervously)

00:02:48.536 --> 00:02:49.630
- Oh, my God.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.206
- [Drew] Okay. So...

00:02:51.206 --> 00:02:54.039
(audience cheers)

00:02:56.512 --> 00:02:58.248
So, Damson...

00:02:59.192 --> 00:03:01.108
I was just wondering.

00:03:01.108 --> 00:03:02.780
I know you're in Prada.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.628
- Oh, my Lord.

00:03:03.628 --> 00:03:05.578
- By the way, my daughter is in crutches,

00:03:05.578 --> 00:03:08.320
so I'm actually really good
at getting people dressed.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.478
(audience laughs)

00:03:09.478 --> 00:03:10.311
So...

00:03:10.311 --> 00:03:11.354
- What is happening right now?

00:03:11.354 --> 00:03:12.187
- I know.

00:03:13.285 --> 00:03:15.298
This is what we do on this show.

00:03:15.298 --> 00:03:17.008
We're silly and we like to have fun.

00:03:17.008 --> 00:03:19.048
And what also is a special connection

00:03:19.048 --> 00:03:20.668
to this particular doll?

00:03:20.668 --> 00:03:23.668
Her name is Courtney but I call
her (high pitched) Courtney,

00:03:24.568 --> 00:03:27.360
because when we lo... Oh, hello?

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.193
(audience whoops)

00:03:31.048 --> 00:03:35.614
- Oh, my God. You're making me blush.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.105
Wow. Look at this.

00:03:37.105 --> 00:03:40.376
(audience applause)

00:03:40.376 --> 00:03:41.209
What is...

00:03:42.782 --> 00:03:45.035
(Damson laughs)

00:03:45.035 --> 00:03:47.264
(audience cheers)

00:03:47.264 --> 00:03:48.097
- So...

00:03:49.588 --> 00:03:51.478
Damson, when we launched our show,

00:03:51.478 --> 00:03:54.128
we launched in the pandemic and

00:03:55.288 --> 00:03:57.688
nobody could come on the show.

00:03:57.688 --> 00:03:58.615
- Oh, wow.

00:03:58.615 --> 00:03:59.458
- And so we didn't have an audience.

00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:01.018
We didn't have guests.

00:04:01.018 --> 00:04:03.300
And I would talk to Courtney a lot.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.288
(audience laugh)

00:04:04.288 --> 00:04:06.991
And I was wondering if
you would marry her.

00:04:08.398 --> 00:04:10.042
- Sure, Courtney.

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:11.848
(Drew laughs)

00:04:11.848 --> 00:04:14.188
- Okay. So what would your sister do?

00:04:14.188 --> 00:04:15.305
Would it be like,

00:04:15.305 --> 00:04:19.648
"Damson, would you take the Courtney,

00:04:19.648 --> 00:04:23.300
to be your lawfully wedded wife?"

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.469
- I do!

00:04:24.469 --> 00:04:26.719
(laughter)

00:04:28.828 --> 00:04:30.268
- And Courtney,

00:04:30.268 --> 00:04:34.108
would you take the dapper,
gentlemanly, talented,

00:04:34.108 --> 00:04:38.848
wonderful Damson, to be your
lawfully wedded husband,

00:04:38.848 --> 00:04:40.588
of which you'd be so lucky?

00:04:40.588 --> 00:04:41.789
- Will you, Courtney?

00:04:41.789 --> 00:04:43.560
- Oh, there's a ring.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.648
You have a ring!

00:04:45.648 --> 00:04:46.940
Oh, my God.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.410
(audience applause)

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.549
Damson Idris.

00:04:50.549 --> 00:04:53.050
The sixth and final season of Snowfall,

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.467
is out now on FX.

00:04:55.429 --> 00:04:56.872
We'll be right back.

00:04:56.872 --> 00:05:01.872
(theme music)
(audience applause)

00:05:01.981 --> 00:05:05.314
(theme music continues)

